#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Bounded adversarial stress harness for packetfin.

Mutates the generated captures in tests/fixtures, runs the release binary over
a fixed option matrix, and classifies every run as ok, crash, hang, rss_limit
or unexpected. Findings are saved with a minimized input and the exact command
that reproduces them.

Usage:
    cargo build --release
    tools/stress                       # 10 minutes, 200k-run cap, seed 1
    tools/stress --minutes 2 --max-cases 5000
    tools/stress --binary path/to/packetfin --out /tmp/pf-stress
    tools/stress --minutes 0 --max-cases 4410000  # complete planned sweep
    tools/stress --self-test
    tools/stress --minutes 10 --memory   # releases also run the memory-ceiling matrix

Modes cover summary, fields, hexdump, detail, JSON, PDML, EK, display-filter
(-Y), stdin (-r -), a -c limit, a 4 KiB state budget and the default
name-resolution path; every mode except "names" passes -n. These are
file-replay modes, so capture writing, live capture (ring buffer and -a
autostop) and -o preferences are not exercised here.

Release gate: a release ships only after a release build runs
`tools/stress --minutes 10` with zero crashes, hangs, rss_limit and unexpected
exits. Report each finding with its reproducer directory and keep it until a
fix and a regression test close it.

Mutation classes per capture: every-byte truncation, all eight bit positions
per byte (a deterministic 256-offset sample above 64 KiB), 24 random
multi-byte edits, and length-field extrema, including compressed-stream
fields, for pcap, pcapng, gzip, zstd and lz4 headers, records, blocks and
trailer lengths. Each fixture contributes at most 400 length mutations. Inputs
are generated in the output directory; the fixture tree is read-only.

--self-test validates fixture discovery, mutation schedule determinism,
truncation and bit-flip coverage, length-mutation serialization, process
classification and RSS limits, output-path safety, bounded campaigns,
reproducer minimization and SIGINT handling, using generated captures and stub
binaries. It needs no packetfin build and does not touch repository fixtures.

Outputs under --out: report.json (machine-readable summary), results.jsonl
(one line per run), and repro/<id>/{case.bin,original.bin,case.json} for each
finding, with the exact command and minimized input. Randomness derives from
--seed, and both --minutes and --max-cases bound the campaign. A time-bounded
campaign samples the byte sweeps; report.json shows planned versus executed
offsets. The default 200,000-run cap also bounds --minutes 0, so a complete
sweep needs an explicit --max-cases (about 4,410,000 for the current fixtures
at seed 1: eight bit flips per byte and twelve modes expand the plan).
Combine --seed with --max-cases for an exactly reproducible sequence. The
first unmutated pass runs every fixture before mutations; use a max-cases
above roughly 600 to reach mutated inputs. Uploads and network access do not
exist.
"""

